Package: STATassist
Title: Standardised Statistical Comparison Workflows
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Wonseok", "Oh", , "hiows97@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0002-0687-8466"))
Description: Runs a family of complementary statistical tests through a single
    consistent function call and returns standardised, feature-wise result
    tables. Two-group comparison reports parametric, rank-based and robust
    results side by side, together with effect estimates, confidence intervals
    and multiplicity adjusted p-values, so that a conclusion is never based on
    a single test. Grouped boxplot visualisation with matching summary
    statistics is included. The implemented methods include those described by
    Welch (1947) <doi:10.1093/biomet/34.1-2.28>, Wilcoxon (1945)
    <doi:10.2307/3001968>, Mann and Whitney (1947)
    <doi:10.1214/aoms/1177730491>, Yuen (1974)
    <doi:10.1093/biomet/61.1.165>, and Brunner and Munzel (2000)
    <doi:10.1002/(SICI)1521-4036(200001)42:1%3C17::AID-BIMJ17%3E3.0.CO;2-U>.
